            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='8800' id='30' type-v2='empty' w='8643' x='6143' y='800'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              <format attr='margin-top' value='6' />
              <format attr='margin-right' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin-bottom' value='6' />
              <format attr='margin-left' value='0' />
              <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='78300' id='151' type-v2='text' w='94286' x='2857' y='12800'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Overview</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This section provides explanations for the key metrics displayed in the dashboard.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>1. Offers Initiated</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The total number of job offers that have been created in the system.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>2. Pending Approval</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The number of offers that have been created but are still awaiting internal approval before they can be sent to candidates.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>3. Pending Acceptance</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The number of offers that have been sent to candidates but are awaiting their decision (accepted or rejected).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>4. Offers Accepted</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The total number of job offers that have been accepted by candidates.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>5. % Offer Accepted</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This metric represents the percentage of offers accepted out of the total offers sent.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>6. % Offer Comp Ratio</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The Offer Comp Ratio is calculated by dividing the offered salary by the mid-range salary for the corresponding job profile(s). If there are multiple profiles, the average mid-range salary is used. To ensure accurate comparisons, all salaries are normalized to an annual basis, regardless of the frequency format used in the data (e.g., hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, etc.).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#da040a' fontsize='11'>Important Considerations:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>- The system allows different salary frequencies to be entered, such as daily, biweekly, weekly, semimonthly,monthly, annual and hourly (based on weekly working hours).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>- In some cases, incorrect data inputs may occur, such as selecting a monthly frequency but entering an annual salary. This will result in the system multiplying the entered salary by 12, leading to an inflated compensation ratio.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>- As a result, certain compensation ratios may appear disproportionately high. These anomalies are typically due to such input errors in salary frequency selection.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#da040a' fontsize='11'>Action Needed:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> Please verify the accuracy of the salary input frequency and ensure it aligns with the actual salary value entered to maintain accurate compensation ratio data.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>7. Offers Rejected</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The total number of job offers that have been rejected by candidates during the reporting period.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>8. % Offers Rejected</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This metric represents the percentage of offers rejected out of the total offers sent.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>9. Hires</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The total number of candidates who have accepted offers and have been officially hired.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>10. No Show</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>The number of candidates who initially accepted a job offer but ultimately did not join the company</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
